Third-party components linked into the oxa binary
-------------------------------------------------

Rust crates are not vendored; Cargo fetches them from crates.io under their own licences and
Cargo.lock pins the exact versions. Two of them embed third-party material in the binary beyond
their own Rust code, and their licence texts ship with oxa:

  QuickJS (QuickJS-ng), through rquickjs-sys: MIT.           Full text: LICENSE-QuickJS.txt
  syntect and its default syntax set (Sublime Text syntax
  definitions, sublimehq/Packages): MIT + the Packages
  permission notice.                                         Full text: LICENSE-syntect.txt

The TLS client behind `web_search` and remote MCP servers (ureq with rustls) brings components
under further licences, some with third-party material inside:

  ring (ISC and Apache-2.0; code derived from BoringSSL and
  OpenSSL), webpki-roots (Mozilla's root certificates,
  CDLA-Permissive-2.0), rustls-webpki and untrusted (ISC),
  subtle (BSD-3-Clause).                                     Full texts: LICENSE-TLS.txt

Other crates in the binary whose licence is not "MIT OR Apache-2.0" or MIT alone: similar
(Apache-2.0), foldhash (Zlib). `cargo tree -p oxa-cli --edges normal --format '{p} {l}'` prints
the licence of every linked crate.
